{"id":"fe671cae538b4196876c8677fc0be0cc","owner":"esri_IN_content0","ownerId":"9a9340ddd2b842f09cd8b54bfaa114fd","created":1754377460000,"modified":1789017959000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"River Streams (India-WRIS)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Requires Subscription","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<p>The River Polyline dataset provides detailed information on 27,575 rivers across India, mapped as polylines with their respective names. This dataset has been sourced from India-WRIS and has been edited using the Imagery basemap available within ArcGIS Online Platform and offers comprehensive coverage of the river network across the country.<\/p><p><strong>Key Uses of the Dataset:<\/strong><br />Hydrological Analysis: Useful for studying river systems, watersheds, and drainage patterns.<\/p><p>Water Resource Management: Helps in planning and managing water resources, irrigation, and flood control measures.<\/p><p>Environmental Studies: Supports research on river basin ecology, habitat conservation, and pollution monitoring.<\/p><p>Infrastructure Planning: Assists in the planning of dams, bridges, flood protection structures, and other water-related infrastructure.<\/p><p>Educational &amp; Research Applications: Ideal for academic studies in geography, hydrology, and environmental sciences.<\/p><p>GIS Applications: Can be directly integrated with GIS platforms for creating thematic maps and conducting spatial analyses.<\/p><p><br />Source: India-WRIS (Water Resources Information System of India), <a target='_blank' href='https://indiawris.gov.in/wris/#/geoSpatialData' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://indiawris.gov.in/wris/#/geoSpatialData<\/a><\/p><p>&nbsp;<\/p>","tags":["Rivers in India","River System","River Names","India","Hydrology","Ministry of Jal Shakti","India WRIS","NWIC","CWC"],"snippet":"The River Name dataset provides information like river's name all over India. Total river's name in this layer is of 27,575 rivers. The India-WRIS (Water Resources Information System) provides data on various river systems across India. Major river systems include the Indus, Ganga, Brahmaputra, Narmada, Tapti, Godavari, Krishna, Cauvery, and Mahanadi. National Water Information Centre (NWIC) 2025","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1754380975383.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[79.077046,21.286491],[79.181528,21.330208]],"categories":["/Categories/Environment/Fresh water","/Categories/Environment/Earth observations"],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Ministry of Jal Shakti, NWIC, India WRIS, CWC, Esri India\n","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><a target='_blank' href='https://indiawris.gov.in/wris/#/termandcondition' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://indiawris.gov.in/wris/#/termandcondition<\/a><\/p><p style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>This work is li